    "raw_public_english_response": "Proposal submitted and accepted. Receipt summary:\n\n- **Case**: `gaussian-pcseg2-materialization-gap` — program `gaussian`, project `gaussian-pcseg2-materialization-gap`\n- **Readiness**: `blocked_missing_evidence`\n- **Normalization**: `raw_contract_valid: true`, no normalization applied, no conflicting explicit setting fields\n- **Settings preserved (source literals)**: functional `B3LYP`, basis `pcseg-2`, `freq: true`; all other fields null/empty\n- **Guards**: `native_input_authored: false`, `command_authored: false`, `project_written: false`, `execution_requested: false`\n\nKey reasoning recorded in the analysis summary:\n\n1. **BSE discovery ≠ deterministic materialization.** `method.basis 'pcseg-2'` is `exact_registered` (capability `gaussian.basis.bse.pcseg2`), loader-accepted and renderer-preserved — but the evidence ceiling is only `loader_renderer_verification_only` (`engine_executed`, `safe_preview_executed`, `scientific_adequacy_verified`, `setting_combination_verified` all false). No exact, request-bound deterministic receipt shows pcseg-2 materializing under Gaussian 16.C01, so the materialization gap blocks the project.\n\n2. **Scope mismatch.** The registry receipt is declared for job kind `opt` only and cannot discharge a `freq` applicability rule.\n\n3. **B3LYP** resolves `exact_registered` (`gaussian.functional.b3lyp`) but carries the same loader/renderer-only evidence ceiling.\n\nNo project writes, native inputs, commands, or execution were performed.",
